A||N||5||Jefrysuko||Limited Use Classic Auto Insurance||||1||
Z||000000||Jefrysuko||05-04-2001||12:46 PM||||Hello all,<BR>       I just wanted to share something about auto insurance with you.  For several years now I have driven my 88 GT during the summer months and parked it during the winter.  During these winter months I would suspend all but the collision coverage on my insurance to save money.  Well last year Paul Vargyas published in the NIFE newsletter that he qualified for "Limited Use Antique/Classic" category of insurance through his local State Farm Insurance Agent.  He has a nice V8 Formula for which his premium was $105 every six months.<BR>       With that information I called my insurance agent today for I was going to take my car out this weekend.  A short talk on the phone and I was able to put my 88 GT in the same category.  My deductibles are now down to $100 the Liability and medical payments etc... are set at their top limits and best yet I raised the value of my car to $7000.  The only limitation I have is that I cannot exceed a yearly mileage of 3500 miles.  My premium is now $82 which is less than half of what it used to be.  <BR>       I will now leave my car insured all year long and when there is a break in the weather during those winter months I believe that I will be taking my Fiero for a ride instead of regretting that I had it in storage.<BR>       Another side note for those of you concerned with EPA testing.  Your state may recognize this type of insurance as applying to a car that is driven infrequently and grant you EXEMPTION.<BR>       I would like to thank Paul Vargyas and the rest of the board members of NIFE for providing this information and helping make owning my Fiero cheaper and more enjoyable (if that is possible :-))<P>Jeffrey D Suckow<P>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||rockcrawl||05-04-2001||03:07 PM||||Don't even bother trying to get specialty car insurance if you're under 26 years old. It's not gonna happen. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||05-04-2001||04:16 PM||||ive checked into a few kitcar, Historical, etc insur companies. One had unlimited annual milage and could insure for whatever limit I wanted. the big but was, It was unlimited milage only to and from shows, parades. If I took it for a nite out with the gf, it wasnt covered. I just kept with my reg insurance because I love driving my car all the time, not just when they tell me I can. Read all your fine print to make sure you know all their rules.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jefrysuko||05-04-2001||04:37 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>ive checked into a few kitcar, Historical, etc insur companies. One had unlimited annual milage and could insure for whatever limit I wanted. the big but was, It was unlimited milage only to and from shows, parades. If I took it for a nite out with the gf, it wasnt covered. I just kept with my reg insurance because I love driving my car all the time, not just when they tell me I can. Read all your fine print to make sure you know all their rules.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I will check things out when I get my paperwork in the mail but I believe that the only major limitation I have is that I can't drive over 3,500 miles.  If I find any more limitations I will let everyone know.  If you don't drive your car daily I would imagine that you don't put more than that on it.  I love driving my car also and that is why I wanted this insurance so that I could drive it whenever I got the desire and not have to put it in "cold" storage.  You might want to check with your regular insurance company to see if they have some other category that will allow you to increase your "replacement/loss value" and still allow you to drive it as you desire.  Alot of times all that is needed to do this is a professional apraisal.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||05-04-2001||08:40 PM||||The one company (forget name) I got the good rate and unlimited miles, said they require it not to be your only vehicle (I have 3), must be garaged (yes) must have garage security system (yes, audio alarm & Video cameras). I almost signed the line when I saw fine print saying driven only to shows, exhibitions, parades. Thats when I called back to check. I asked if I wanted to take it out for dinner or a date if there was any problem. They told me no, couldnt use it for any kind of reg transportation. Needless to say, i said bye bye, no thanks. My current insurance company took pictures to file, and said it would cover the cars blue book value plus all receipts I kept, like body kit, wheels, interior, engine, etc. All for like replacement value and not depreciated prices.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||fierofreek2001||05-04-2001||09:00 PM||||i work at geico and we do insure classic cars,... but the guidelines are very strict and very few people qualify... here are the guidelines i can think of off the top of my head<BR>1. Car must be over 15 years old<BR>2. All licensed drivers in the household must have 10 years driving experience<BR>3. No tickets/violations/accidents in last 5 years ( approx. .. i cant remember exact time frames)<BR>4. All Drivers must have a regular use vehicle 15 years or newer.<BR>5. Classic car is only allowed to go to carshows/ parades/ exhibitions... no joy riding at all!!!<BR>6. Must be in locked enclosure when not in use...<BR>7. Car must be at least 98% restored...<BR>8. No major custom engine mods... <BR>9. Car can not be driven over 3000 miles a year<BR>10. At Geico, you must have an existing auto policy also<P><BR>Thats about all i can think of for now.. as you read this.. you might already see that you dont qualify.... surprise surprise.. we hardly ever make classic car sales...<BR>hope some of this helps!.. dont blame me for the gay rules, i just work there  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Steve||||reg||1
